Sources for `harness-evolution` skill (see plans/skill-audits/harness-evolution.md for full audit):

- citypaul/.dotfiles self-evolution discipline — inspiration, manual edits over time.
- Kieran Klaassen (EveryInc) compound-engineering — inspiration for auto-capture pattern, adapted with HITL gate.
- Boris Cherny "how Boris uses Claude Code" — https://howborisusesclaudecode.com — reference.

Strategy: original. No existing precedent for this exact mechanism (inbound feedback + outbound audit, HITL strict). Author from first principles.

Inbound feedback files a GitHub issue directly via `gh issue create` (no bespoke
CLI subcommand; the issue tracker is the queue). See issue #35 / docs/DECISIONS.md
(2026-06-26) for why the `.void/harness-feedback/proposed/` queue + `feedback push`
were dropped.

Companion CLI subcommand:
- npx @voidcorp/harness audit

Shared util: packages/core/claude/lib/usage-log.ts (≤ 30 LOC, local-only logging).
